    Replace periodic-stable-jobs with local job list.
    
    The shared periodic-stable-jobs template in openstack-zuul-jobs runs
    openstack-tox-py310 on stable/2025.2, but kolla-ansible on this branch
    sets python_requires >= 3.11 and its ansible-core requirement carries
    a python_version >= '3.11' marker. The py310 tox environment therefore
    cannot install kolla-ansible at all and the job has failed on every
    run. In the 30 days to 2026-07-01 that was 30 failures from 30 runs in
    the periodic-stable pipeline, pure noise for anyone watching the
    periodic dashboards.
    
    Zuul templates cannot exclude individual jobs, so replace the shared
    template with an explicit periodic-stable job list running what the
    shared template would have run minus the impossible interpreter: docs
    and py312. This mirrors the approach already taken for check and gate
    on this branch with the local openstack-python3-jobs-kolla-ansible
    template, which exists precisely to skip py310 jobs.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5 (1M context, medium effort)
